# Line-ending policy (T192).
#
# Every committed blob in this repository is LF. Without this file a Windows
# checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` materialises CRLF working copies, and four
# committed tests in scripts/ci/ read the REAL packaging/docker/Dockerfile and
# packaging/nix/flake.nix through `\n`-anchored regexes, so they fail locally
# while passing on CI's Linux checkout. `oxfmt --check .` went red on ~2361 of
# 2369 files for the same reason. The cost is not those four tests: it is that
# the local signal is dead, so a real regression hiding among the noise is
# invisible to the next person who runs the suite.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalises on commit and checks out LF on every platform.
# It changes no committed blob — they are already LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries: never touched, on any platform.
*.png binary
*.ttf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.onnx binary
*.jar binary
*.keystore binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.mp3 binary
*.wav binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary

# Lockfiles are generated; keep them out of diffs but still LF-normalised.
package-lock.json -diff
